Corpus v2 review: seams need one call, bleeds need audible windows, one voice per person

shape() R4 now counts a system/browser pair only when both carry the same call over
the overlap (voice, phase, noise bed, bleeds), and the D49 overlap must carry it on
both sides of callConnected. R6 checks every bleed's windows (source speaking,
target present) and needs an echo audible where the target is quiet in each
direction; each person speaks one pinned voice. New data mutations cover the review
probes (wrong seam partner, phase/seed mutants, system stopping at callConnected,
empty/silent/masked bleeds, two voices for source-a); each passed the old shape().

The stored-WAV checks derive the identical-overlap pairs from shape()'s seam() and
check every expected bleed as target minus its own carrier, b-return into the mic
under my speech included. Floor mutants the corpus cannot show (gap masking over
non-zero samples, mean removal) must fail synthetic oracle checks; span ignoring
ownership joins the corpus mutants. The schema checker loads lazily, so the digest
pin runs on a bare python3, and Noise.held asserts windows start at their origin.

